VACUUM FREEZE;

But, the DB level above command will run as single process, table by table, take long time and without guarantee the DB age lower down, you have to identify the efficient way to freeze certain table to make the age drop down. 

0. Get all the old age table info 
SELECT
    n.nspname, c.relname, age(c.relfrozenxid) AS xid_age, pg_total_relation_size(c.oid)/1024/1024/1024 AS GB 
FROM pg_class c
JOIN pg_namespace n
    ON n.oid = c.relnamespace
WHERE c.relkind = 'r'
ORDER BY age(c.relfrozenxid) DESC
LIMIT 50;

1. Pre-cleanup the small tables first
SELECT
    n.nspname, c.relname, age(c.relfrozenxid) AS xid_age, pg_total_relation_size(c.oid)/1024/1024/1024 AS GB
FROM pg_class c
JOIN pg_namespace n
    ON n.oid = c.relnamespace
WHERE c.relkind = 'r' and pg_total_relation_size(c.oid)/1024/1024/1024<1
ORDER BY age(c.relfrozenxid) DESC
LIMIT 50;

-- Generate command (Should run it as routine) 
SELECT 'vacuum (freeze,analyze,verbose) '||n.nspname||'.'||c.relname||';' 
FROM pg_class c
JOIN pg_namespace n
    ON n.oid = c.relnamespace
WHERE c.relkind = 'r' and pg_total_relation_size(c.oid)/1024/1024/1024<1
ORDER BY age(c.relfrozenxid) DESC
LIMIT 50;

